---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - Pink Coding Club" isIndex={false} showHero={false}>
  <div class="page-container">
    
    <!-- Sidebar Navigation -->
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <nav class="side-nav">
        <a href="#about" class="nav-link active" data-target="about">ABOUT</a>
        <a href="#business" class="nav-link" data-target="business">BUSINESS</a>
        <a href="#contact" class="nav-link" data-target="contact">CONTACT</a>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="content-wrapper">
      
      <!-- ABOUT SECTION -->
      <section id="about" class="content-section">
        <h1 class="pink-title">ABOUT</h1>
        <div class="text-block">
          <p>As a young girl, Rachel always hated coding and thought it was the most milquetoast of things. Finding chatbots that asked for pizza preferences mundane, she gave up on coding and wanted nothing to do with it. Only when she reached adulthood, she realized coding was another creative medium like fashion or poetry, and that schools separated the arts and STEM when they should been taught to be connected. </p>
          <br>
          <p>But after hearing many personal anecdotes where women stripped themselves of their femineity to feel accepted by the tech community, Rachel knew there was something awry with the current culture. So then, disillusioned by the education system and tech industry, Rachel created the Pink Coding Club to counter the hyper-masculine and uninviting world of tech. Pink Coding Club does not only educate through art and fashion, but empowers the "girly girl" and helps her remember that she does have a place in technology whether others like it or not. </p>
          <br>
          <p>The hyper-feminine perspective in technology is valuable not only for its impeccable design, but for its insights in representation, accessibility, and trauma-minded design. Every single one of her designs is not only made with love, but pure passion as well. This perspective changes the game and goes beyond simply creating trends. </p>
        <br>
        <p>Transcending far beyond just education, P.C.C. marks itself as rebellion in the industry, carving a path for the next generation of girls. Unapologetically herself, a P.C.C. member is not only an innovator, but defines the future of technology. She can design. She can create. She can do anything. She leads the culture.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="sub-title">Our Principles</h2>
        <ul class="principles-list">
          <li><strong>Individuality</strong> — We celebrate the unique ideas, backgrounds, and strengths of every member.</li>
          <li><strong>Innovation</strong> — We develop original ideas, solve problems creatively, and collaborate with people around the world.</li>
          <li><strong>Trauma-Informed Design</strong> — Like the Hippocratic oath in medicine, we strive to do no harm, protect users, respect their privacy, and take responsibility for the technology we create.</li>
          <li><strong>Respect</strong> — We respect different ideas, identities, experiences, and ways of learning.</li>
          <li><strong>Integrity</strong> — When something is inaccurate, unsafe, or harmful, we take responsibility and work diligently to fix it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="faq-title">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</h3>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-summary">
              <span>What is Pink Coding Club?</span>
              <span class="plus">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-summary">
              <span>Is learning at Pink Coding Club free?</span>
              <span class="plus">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-summary">
              <span>Do I need to attend weekly classes?</span>
              <span class="plus">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- BUSINESS SECTION -->
      <section id="business" class="content-section">
        <h1 class="pink-title">BUSINESS</h1>
      </section>

      <!-- CONTACT SECTION -->
      <section id="contact" class="content-section">
        <h1 class="pink-title">CONTACT</h1>
        
        <div class="contact-grid">
          <div class="contact-col">
            <h4>OFFICE</h4>
            <p>Somewhere,<br>Over the Rainbow</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="contact-col">
            <h4>EMAIL</h4>
            <p><a href="mailto:soontocome@pinkcodingclub.com" class="email-link">soontocome@pinkcodingclub.com</a></p>
            
            <h4 class="mt-8">Where to Find Us</h4>
            <div class="media-kit-buttons">
              <button class="outline-btn">Instagram</button>
              <button class="outline-btn">TikTok</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    const sections = document.querySelectorAll(".content-section");
    const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll(".nav-link");

    const observerOptions = {
      root: null,
      rootMargin: "0px",
      threshold: 0.3 
    };

    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          navLinks.forEach((link) => {
            link.classList.remove("active");
            if (link.getAttribute("data-target") === entry.target.id) {
              link.classList.add("active");
            }
          });
        }
      });
    }, observerOptions);

    sections.forEach((section) => {
      observer.observe(section);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .page-container {
    display: flex;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 120px 2rem 4rem 2rem;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  }

  /* Sidebar Styling */
  .sidebar {
    width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .side-nav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 100px; 
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .nav-link {
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
    color: #555555;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .nav-link:hover, .nav-link.active {
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* Main Content Wrapper */
  .content-wrapper {
    flex-grow: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }

  .content-section {
    padding-bottom: 8rem;
    min-height: 80vh;
    scroll-margin-top: 120px; 
  }

  .pink-title {
    font-family: 'Archivo Black', sans-serif;
    font-size: 5rem;
    color: #facee2;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -2px;
  }

  .text-block p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #d1d1d1;
    text-transform: none; 
  }

  .sub-title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Archivo Black', sans-serif;
  }

  .principles-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .principles-list li {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #222;
    color: #d1d1d1;
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .principles-list li strong {
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* FAQ Accordion Styling */
  .faq-title {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .faq-summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
    list-style: none; /* Hide standard marker */
  }

  .faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none; /* Hide WebKit marker */
  }

  .faq-summary:hover {
    color: #facee2;
  }

  .plus {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .plus {
    transform: rotate(45px); /* Rotates '+' into an 'x' on open */
    color: #facee2;
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #a0a0a0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* Contact Section Styling */
  .contact-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
  }

  .contact-col h4 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: #888;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .contact-col p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #e0e0e0;
  }

  .email-link {
    color: #ffffff;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .mt-8 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .media-kit-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .outline-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #444;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .outline-btn:hover {
    border-color: #facee2;
    color: #facee2;
  }

  /* Mobile Responsiveness */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-container {
      padding: 100px 1rem 2rem 1rem; 
    }

    .sidebar {
      width: 30px;
    }

    .side-nav {
      top: 90px;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .nav-link {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    }

    .content-wrapper {
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }

    .content-section {
      scroll-margin-top: 90px;
    }

    .pink-title {
      font-size: 3rem;
    }

    .contact-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
